</figure>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ When and How do LRMs use Latent Thoughts (§ )? ‣ Appendix B Statistical Evaluation ‣ Observable Patterns Are Not Explanations:A Causal-Geometric Analysis of Latent Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> reports results for the latent thought ablation at test-time experiment; Tables <a href="#A2.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ When and How do LRMs use Latent Thoughts (§ )? ‣ Appendix B Statistical Evaluation ‣ Observable Patterns Are Not Explanations:A Causal-Geometric Analysis of Latent Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> &amp; <a href="#A2.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ When and How do LRMs use Latent Thoughts (§ )? ‣ Appendix B Statistical Evaluation ‣ Observable Patterns Are Not Explanations:A Causal-Geometric Analysis of Latent Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> (prompt and thought-positions respectively) for the causal-tracing experiment; and Tables <a href="#A2.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ When and How do LRMs use Latent Thoughts (§ )? ‣ Appendix B Statistical Evaluation ‣ Observable Patterns Are Not Explanations:A Causal-Geometric Analysis of Latent Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> &amp; <a href="#A2.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ When and How do LRMs use Latent Thoughts (§ )? ‣ Appendix B Statistical Evaluation ‣ Observable Patterns Are Not Explanations:A Causal-Geometric Analysis of Latent Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> (ablation and amplification respectively) for the gradient-subspace interventions experiment.</p>
</div>
</section>
