<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 15: </span>Hyperparameters used to train the GPT-2 CODI models.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Model size.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All GPT-2 models are built on the pretrained GPT-2 small (<math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="124" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>124</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">124</annotation></semantics></math>M parameters; <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Radford et al., 2019</a></cite>). CODI uses LoRA fine-tuning (rank <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math>) on these backbones; all other models are fully fine-tuned. Full per-model, per-task hyperparameters appear in Tables <a href="#A3.T14" title="Table 14 ‣ C.3 Training Details ‣ Appendix C Models, Controls, and Training Details ‣ Observable Patterns Are Not Explanations:A Causal-Geometric Analysis of Latent Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> and <a href="#A3.T15" title="Table 15 ‣ C.3 Training Details ‣ Appendix C Models, Controls, and Training Details ‣ Observable Patterns Are Not Explanations:A Causal-Geometric Analysis of Latent Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</article>
